        "date": "2026-11-08T10:08:47Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui): a ball nose's corner radius is its ball - shown, not edited\n\nA ball nose's tip is a sphere, so its corner radius is half the\ndiameter, and every reader already used that number whatever the field\nheld (Cutter::of, Tool::profile, the stock sim's sphere atom). The tool\neditor still offered an editable \"Corner radius\" that changed nothing,\nand a draft retyped from an end mill saved a ball with corner 0.\n\n- Tool::tip_corner_r states the law: a ball's (or probe's) corner is\n  d/2, every other kind answers its own field.\n- The editor shows the ball's corner as text with no field to edit.\n- ToolUi::to_tool saves a ball with corner_r = d/2, so the document\n  says what is cut; ToolUi::tool_kind names the draft's kind.\n- The library summary reads tip_corner_r.\n\nFixes #263\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
